# Wave W17-R (Route 126): crater rock — crater-wall rock standing in the lane’s water: a warm grey wall-rock drawn in massive joints — few blocks, wide dark seams — the crater’s own masonry at water level, foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: the crater wall rising huge from the bay). Route 126’s own rock — split from Craterlake town’s craterfloor street by register (wild wall vs city floor) and from Route 125’s frost-fringed isle rock by the massive jointing and the warmth: no ice stands on the crater’s rock.
